          "blockId": "BLK_GU_JEEMAIN2027_PHY_BACFBE4A_CONCEPTS_01",
          "semanticAnchorId": "ANCHOR__BACFBE4A_1",
          "title": "1. Key Academic Principles: The Universal Law of Gravitation, Gravitational Constant",
          "contentMarkdown": "Newton's Universal Law of Gravitation states that the attractive force between two masses is F = G * (m1 * m2) / r^2. The Universal Gravitational Constant G has the value 6.674 x 10^-11 N*m^2 / kg^2 with dimensions [M^-1 L^3 T^-2]. Gravitational force between two particles is an attractive central force that acts along the line joining their centres.",
          "boundAtomicFactIds": [
            "AF_GU_JEEMAIN2027_PHY_BACFBE4A_5C60A7A0",
            "AF_GU_JEEMAIN2027_PHY_BACFBE4A_BFD5EC35",
